    "title": "EFV CNS toxicity: insomnia and vivid dreams",
    "message": "Guidelines list persistent CNS toxicity including insomnia and abnormal dreams as EFV adverse events requiring management. Patient has been on EFV for ~23 months and reports poor sleep and vivid dreams for several weeks. EFV is a well-recognized cause of these symptoms. No alternative cause is documented. Guidelines note EFV 400 mg has fewer adverse events than EFV 600 mg, and DTG-based regimens are preferred first-line. The clinician's plan documents the complaint but proposes no management action.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Consider substituting EFV with DTG, or switching to EFV 400 mg if DTG is contraindicated. Perform viral load test if substituting after six months on ART.",
