    "alert_id": "ALERT_002",
    "title": "No renal or hepatic monitoring on TDF regimen",
    "message": "Guidelines state that for TDF toxicity, LFTs and RFTs should be done. Patient is on TDF but no renal function tests or liver function tests are recorded. TDF can cause chronic kidney disease, acute kidney injury, Fanconi syndrome, and hepatotoxicity. Absence of baseline or follow-up renal and hepatic labs represents a monitoring gap that could allow silent toxicity to progress undetected.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Order renal function tests (creatinine, urinalysis) and liver function tests for patient on TDF-based regimen.",
