    "title": "Low-level viremia on current regimen",
    "message": "Guidelines address low-level viremia, noting viral load above suppression thresholds carries risk of subsequent virologic non-suppression and treatment failure. Patient's latest viral load is 60 copies/mL, indicating low-level viremia rather than full suppression. This may signal early adherence issues or emerging resistance, particularly relevant given concurrent EFV CNS toxicity that could impair adherence.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Repeat viral load to confirm trend. Assess adherence and consider regimen review if viremia persists or worsens.",
